                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_308">Stafford. Augustinian
                        priory of St Thomas the Martyr. </orgName><p>'Dompnus Eudo de Mere fecit
                        scribere hunc librum et dedit domui beati thome martyris. Anima eius et
                        anima patris eius Gervasii et omnium fidelium anime per misericordiam dei
                        requiescat in pace. Amen'.</p><p>MRJ suggested that this was the abbey of St
                        Thomas of Lesnes (called also Westwood) near Woolwich. Listed under Lessness
                        in MLGB 2nd edn (1964) on basis of ex dono inscription to house of St Thomas
                        the Martyr, but Stafford is perhaps more likely: see N. R. Ker, 'The English
                        manuscripts of the Moralia of Gregory the Great', in Kunsthistorische
                        Forschungen Otto Pächt zu seinem 70. Geburtstag (Salzburg 1972), pp.
                        77--89.</p><p>Medieval binding.</p><p> </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">On fol. 2r scribbled: Many [?]
                     Perkins.</provenance>
